                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d0069c37-1db8-3cce-8d12-f267af4aab3a",
                        "entry_id": "580608cc-6e6b-3f2d-8963-a5990dcb67b6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A low or quiet voice."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6da6466f-6025-46ca-8f17-92a460f24f1c",
                                "sense_id": "d0069c37-1db8-3cce-8d12-f267af4aab3a",
                                "text": "Her sensations were indefinable, and so were they a few minutes afterwards upon hearing Henry Crawford, who had a chair between herself and Tom, ask the latter in an under voice whether there were any plan for resuming the play after the present happy interruption […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "de90de34-f106-4937-9745-430ccba0809b",
                                "sense_id": "d0069c37-1db8-3cce-8d12-f267af4aab3a",
                                "text": "Brayder introduced them to one or two of the men, hastily and in rather an undervoice, as a thing to get over."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ce14b90-8360-4552-86c3-f8a9f7d4d6db",
                                "sense_id": "d0069c37-1db8-3cce-8d12-f267af4aab3a",
                                "text": "A thousand soft undervoices that jumped my jangled senses from his last, weakly syllabled wind to a mosaic of voices within voices, each one immanent in the other, none his but all strangely his […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "853d89ca-721b-4c85-8597-afe5196fbe6b",
                                "sense_id": "d0069c37-1db8-3cce-8d12-f267af4aab3a",
                                "text": "Through the battered century of world wars and massive violence by other means, there had always been an undervoice that spoke through the cannon fire and ack-ack and that sometimes grew strong enough to merge with the battle sounds. It was the struggle between the state and secret groups of insurgents, state-born, wild-eyed—the anarchists, terrorists, assassins and revolutionaries who tried to bring about apocalyptic change."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "eeb6e4c6-c156-4201-86a9-b2b780b6f0ef",
                                "sense_id": "d0069c37-1db8-3cce-8d12-f267af4aab3a",
                                "text": "[…] Your mother\nPlayed Prospero, flying her magic in\nTo stage the Masque, and bless the marriage,\nEavesdropping on the undervoices\nOf the honeymooners in Paris […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
